//! The stock root's plan for an image: what an image description whose root
//! is the stock root comes to once its processes are bound to their
//! declarations (`sosimage.imagefile.bind`), the checks it is held to, and the
//! module `imageplan` the builder writes for root's build in `bootplan`'s
//! terms (`root/bootplan`).
//!
//! The region table's rows, which are root's boot set (spec §12): one image
//! blob per process, one destination per process, then a row per device, in
//! the order the image first uses each (every window need of each process, in
//! image order and declaration order, then each `[[setup]]` write's device),
//! then a row per pool, in `[[pool]]` order, then a row per heap's pool, in
//! image order and each declaration's slot order (`Bindings.heaps`). A row is
//! tagged with its ordinal.
//!
//! Each process's records, in its declaration's order, each under its tag:
//! its `system` record is a sibling of root's System that keeps the rights
//! the declaration names, or the image's default (`ImageFile.system_rights`,
//! which an image that names a console withholds `debug` from) when it names
//! none, carried by name (`bootplan.RightName`); a whole `window` is the row
//! of the device it is bound to, given to the last process that takes that
//! row whole when no carve of it follows, and a sibling of it for every
//! other; a `part` window is a carve of its device's row; a `line` is the
//! bound device's interrupt line, which root binds; a `serve` is the server
//! end of a connection of its own, and a `client` an inlet of the connection
//! of the serve it is bound to; a `memory` record is its pool's row. In an
//! image that names a console (`[image] console`), every process but the one
//! serving it is given one record more, after its declared ones: an inlet of
//! the console's connection under `bootplan.CONSOLE_TAG`, which raises the
//! handles it holds when it starts by one. Each heap it declares is given
//! last, its pool's row under `bootplan.HEAP_TAG` plus the heap's slot
//! (`Source.Heap`), which root gives with the launch convention's mask for a
//! heap's pool (spec §12). Its quota rows are its
//! declaration's `[quota]`, each replaced by the image's `quota` for it,
//! which may raise a row and not lower it.
//!
//! A declaration with `[ceilings]` gives its process one ceiling word for
//! each kind of `sosimage.rights`, the rights the table lists for it and none
//! for a kind it leaves out, which root narrows the process's to before it
//! gives it anything; one without gives none. Each record carries a keep word
//! (`Declaration.keep_word`): the rights its declaration names, else its
//! kind's ceiling when it has `[ceilings]`, else every right. The console's
//! inlet is the `pipe-inlet` ceiling's, which is refused when it lacks `post`
//! (`check_console_inlet`).
//!
//! A declaration's `bands` gives its process's band map, carried as the
//! packed word the kernel's `BandMap` op takes: `bootplan.FULL_BANDS` for
//! `full`, `bootplan.SIMPLE_BANDS` otherwise, for which root sets nothing.
//! A client whose `Normal` level is above its server's, a declared client or
//! the console's inlet's holder, is refused (`check_bands`): the convention
//! that stands in for a server inheriting its client's level across a pipe is
//! that no client outranks its server. The two stock maps put `Normal` at 2,
//! so the check holds a map the plan carries from elsewhere.
//!
//! A `[[setup]]` write carves from its device's row the window of the board's
//! grain (four bytes at least) that holds its register, and writes the
//! register at its offset into that window.
//!
//! Refused by name: a line two processes need, which the kernel binds once; a
//! `line` need bound to a device with no line; an image `quota` row below its
//! declaration's; and an image `threads` row of 0, since a process's first
//! thread is charged to it. Against the kernel (`check_plan`): a `handles` row
//! past the longest handle table, a `mappings` row past the grant rows an image
//! leaves, a row at the ledger's unlimited mark, a row the image alone gives
//! below the row the image's children start with (an image raises a row and
//! never lowers one), a child whose `Handle` row is short of what it holds when
//! it starts and once its heaps have grown (the console's inlet included, so a
//! row at the declaration's own floor is short in an image that names a
//! console), a child whose `Mapping` row is short of a row for each window and
//! each heap, or whose `Memory` row is short of one for each heap; a step at
//! which root would hold more handles than the longest table has or make more
//! objects of a kind than the image's slab of it holds: Process objects (root
//! and each child), Pipe objects (one per connection), Interrupt objects (one
//! per line) and IoMemory objects (one per device row, carve given and setup
//! write's carve); and more Memory objects than the image's slab holds, one per
//! row of the region table that is not a device's and one for each heap's
//! `Memory`. A heap's shares are its program's to budget, and are not counted.
//!
//! Root's arena (`root_arena`) is what its heap takes for the plan: each of
//! the plan's vectors and of root's own bookkeeping is made once at its
//! length (`root/src/main.saw`), so the sum of their blocks, the heap's
//! control block and `ROOT_ARENA_MARGIN`, never below `ROOT_ARENA_FLOOR`,
//! serves every allocation root makes. An element's words are `bootplan`'s,
//! which root's compile holds to the types' sizes.
//!
//! A test image states a plan of its own, unchecked, as JSON
//! (`ImagePlan.read`), so a case can reach each of the stock root's stops:
//!
//!     {
//!       "connections": 1,
//!       "children": [{"name": "first", "image": 0, "destination": 1,
//!                     "start": 1, "shutdown": false,
//!                     "quota": {"waiters": 1},
//!                     "records": [{"tag": 1, "source": "system"},
//!                                 {"tag": 2, "source": "carve", "from": 4,
//!                                  "offset": 12, "len": 4}]}],
//!       "setup": [{"register": "RTC.ALARM_HIGH", "row": 4, "offset": 12,
//!                  "len": 4, "at": 0, "op": "set", "value": 90}]
//!     }
//!
//! A record's `from`, `offset`, `len` and `keep` (every right), a child's
//! `quota`, `ceilings` (an object of a kind's key and the word its ceiling is
//! narrowed to, as the plan carries it), `bands` (the packed map root sets,
//! the simple one when left out), `records` and `shutdown`, and
//! `children`, `connections` and `setup` may be left out (zero, none, false);
//! an unknown key is refused. A test plan may also state
//! `windows`, the count of windows root is given in place of the one the
//! builder makes (`window_rows`), so a case can hand root a count that is
//! short. A test image's child keeps
//! the launch convention's System rights (`child_rights`).

import toml.{TomlPosition}
import bootplan.{FULL_BANDS, SIMPLE_BANDS, CHILD_WORDS, QUOTA_WORDS, CEILING_WORDS, RECORD_WORDS, RIGHT_WORDS, SETUP_WORDS,
                 PROCESS_WORDS, ENDS_WORDS, ROW_TAG_WORDS, ROW_WINDOW_WORDS, CONSOLE_TAG,
                 HEAP_TAG, KEEP_ALL}
import sosimage.board.{Board, Window, quota_keys}
import sosimage.declaration.{Declaration, RecordKind, child_rights}
import sosimage.failure.{BuildError}
import sosimage.fields.{Fields}
import sosimage.heapsize.{HEAP_CLASS_WORDS, HEAP_CONTROL_FIXED, heap_classes}
import sosimage.hex.{hex}
import sosimage.imagefile.{Bindings, ImageFile, SetupOp}
import sosimage.kernel.{KernelFacts, MEMORIES, QUOTA_HANDLE, QUOTA_KINDS,
                        QUOTA_MAPPING, QUOTA_MEMORY, SLAB_KINDS, THREADS}
import sosimage.limits.{PlanNeeds, QUOTA_UNLIMITED, quota_slab}
import sosimage.regions.{RegionKind}
import sosimage.rights.{CEILING_KINDS, ceiling_kind_at, ceiling_kind, right_word}
import sosimage.rules.{refused}

/// The handles root holds at boot before its rows' (spec §12): System,
/// Process and Thread.
static ROOT_BOOT_HANDLES: Int = 3

/// The handles `sosmain`'s start-up derives for root before `main` runs: its
/// Process handle and its main thread's own Thread handle.
static ROOT_START_HANDLES: Int = 2


/// `QuotaKind.Thread`'s value.
static QUOTA_THREAD: Int = 0

/// What root's arena keeps past the blocks its plan and bookkeeping take.
public static ROOT_ARENA_MARGIN: Int = 256

/// The least arena root is linked with, the user scripts' default.
public static ROOT_ARENA_FLOOR: Int = 0x1000

/// The multiple root's arena is rounded up to: the user scripts align the
/// arena's start and end to 16 bytes.
static ARENA_ALIGN: Int = 16

/// The least window a setup write carves: one register.
static REGISTER_BYTES: UInt64 = 4

/// What a record is made from (`bootplan.Source`).
public enum Source {
    case System,
    case Row,
    case Sibling,
    case Carve,
    case Line,
    case Outlet,
    case Inlet,
    case Heap
}

@synthesize
extension Source: Equatable {}

/// A source's case name in `bootplan.Source`.
public func source_word(source: Source) -> String {
    match source {
        case System -> "System",
        case Row -> "Row",
        case Sibling -> "Sibling",
        case Carve -> "Carve",
        case Line -> "Line",
        case Outlet -> "Outlet",
        case Inlet -> "Inlet",
        case Heap -> "Heap"
    }
}

/// `bootplan.RightName`'s case for a right as a declaration names it, which
/// is one of `child_rights()`.
func right_word(name: String) -> String {
    if name.equals("debug") { return "Debug" }
    if name.equals("process-self") { return "ProcessSelf" }
    if name.equals("clock-get") { return "ClockGet" }
    if name.equals("transfer") { return "Transfer" }
    panic("`{name}` is not a right the declaration reader admits")
}

/// The source a test image's plan names.
func source_named(word: String) -> Source? {
    if word.equals("system") { return Source.System }
    if word.equals("row") { return Source.Row }
    if word.equals("sibling") { return Source.Sibling }
    if word.equals("carve") { return Source.Carve }
    if word.equals("line") { return Source.Line }
    if word.equals("outlet") { return Source.Outlet }
    if word.equals("inlet") { return Source.Inlet }
    if word.equals("heap") { return Source.Heap }
    None
}

/// One record a child is given.
public struct PlanRecord {
    tag: Int
    source: Source
    /// A row's tag, a line, or a connection's index, by `source`.
    from: UInt64
    offset: UInt64
    len: UInt64
    /// The rights the child keeps of it (`bootplan.Record`).
    keep: UInt32
}

/// One of a child's rights ceilings, by `bootplan.CeilingKind`'s case.
public struct PlanCeiling {
    kind: String
    rights: UInt32
}

/// One quota row, by `QuotaKind` value.
public struct PlanQuota {
    kind: Int
    limit: Int
    /// Whether the process's declaration states the row; one only the image
    /// gives may not lower the row the image's children start with.
    declared: Bool
}

/// One child.
public struct PlanChild {
    name: String
    image: Int
    destination: Int
    quota: Vector<PlanQuota>
    /// The ceilings root narrows its own to: one for each kind of
    /// `sosimage.rights` when its declaration has `[ceilings]`, else none.
    ceilings: Vector<PlanCeiling>
    /// The band map root sets on it: `SIMPLE_BANDS` sets none.
    bands: UInt32
    records: Vector<PlanRecord>
    /// The rights its System record keeps, by the names a declaration writes.
    rights: Vector<String>
    start: Int
    shutdown: Bool
    /// The handles it holds when it starts and once its heaps have grown
    /// (`Declaration.handle_floor`, and one for the console's inlet when it is
    /// given one); 0 for a test image's child, which nothing holds to it.
    floor: Int
    /// Its window records and its heaps, each a `Mapping` row it spends, and
    /// each heap a `Memory` row; 0 for a test image's child.
    windows: Int
    heaps: Int
}

@synthesize
extension PlanChild: ExplicitCopy {}

/// One setup write.
public struct PlanSetup {
    register: String
    row: Int
    offset: UInt64
    len: UInt64
    at: UInt64
    op: SetupOp
    value: UInt64
}

/// A row after the blobs and destinations: a device's or a pool's.
public struct PlanRow {
    what: String
    kind: RegionKind
    /// A device row's window; a pool's is placed with the processes.
    base: UInt64
    len: UInt64
    /// The pool a pool row is; "" for a device row and a heap's pool.
    pool: String
    /// The heap whose pool a row is, PROCESS.HEAP; "" for any other row.
    heap: String
    /// The range a heap's pool lies in; "" for any other row.
    ram: String
}

/// An image's plan.
public struct ImagePlan {
    children: Vector<PlanChild>
    setup: Vector<PlanSetup>
    connections: Int
    /// The rows after the blobs and destinations, in order.
    rows: Vector<PlanRow>
    /// The count of windows a test plan states for root, unchecked; root is
    /// otherwise given `window_rows`.
    windows: Int?
}

@synthesize
extension ImagePlan: ExplicitCopy {}

/// The objects of the kinds the stock root makes for a plan that an image's
/// slabs hold: Process (root and each child), Pipe (one per connection),
/// Interrupt (one per line) and IoMemory (one per device row, carve given and
/// setup write's carve). The slabs that hold the rest are derived
/// (`sosimage.limits.plan_limits`).
public struct PlanSlabs {
    processes: Int
    pipes: Int
    interrupts: Int
    iomemories: Int
}

/// The `QuotaKind` value a quota key names.
public func quota_of(key: String) -> Int {
    if key.equals("threads") { return 0 }
    if key.equals("events") { return 1 }
    if key.equals("waiters") { return 2 }
    if key.equals("timers") { return 3 }
    if key.equals("memories") { return 4 }
    if key.equals("iomemories") { return 5 }
    if key.equals("mappings") { return 6 }
    if key.equals("handles") { return 7 }
    8
}

/// `bootplan.QuotaName`'s case for a `QuotaKind` value.
func quota_name(kind: Int) -> String {
    match kind {
        case 0 -> "Thread",
        case 1 -> "Event",
        case 2 -> "Waiter",
        case 3 -> "Timer",
        case 4 -> "Memory",
        case 5 -> "IoMemory",
        case 6 -> "Mapping",
        case 7 -> "Handle",
        case _ -> "Pipe"
    }
}

/// The quota key of a `QuotaKind` value.
func quota_key(kind: Int) -> String {
    let keys = quota_keys()
    var i = 0
    while i < keys.len() {
        let key = keys.get(i) ?? ""
        if quota_of(key) == kind {
            return key
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    "?"
}

/// The tag of the row named `what` in `rows`, after `first` blob and
/// destination rows.
func row_tag(rows: &Vector<PlanRow>, first: Int, device: String, pool: String) -> Int? {
    var i = 0
    while i < rows.len() {
        let r = rows.get(i)!
        if (not device.is_empty() && r.kind == RegionKind.Device && r.what.equals(device)) ||
           (not pool.is_empty() && r.pool.equals(pool)) {
            return first + i
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    None
}

/// The plan of a stock-root image, from its processes' declarations (`decls`,
/// one per process, in order) and what binding them found (`bound`), on
/// `board`, whose protection grain is `grain`.
public func plan_image(image: &ImageFile, board: &Board, decls: &Vector<Declaration>,
                       bound: &Bindings, grain: UInt64) -> Result<ImagePlan, BuildError> {
    let file = image.file
    let count = image.processes.len()
    let first = 2 * count

    // The device rows, in first-use order, then the pool rows.
    var rows = Vector<PlanRow>()
    var p = 0
    while p < count {
        let process = image.processes.get(p)!
        borrow let d = decls[p] {
            var r = 0
            while r < d.records.len() {
                let record = d.records.get(r)!
                r = r + 1
                if record.kind != RecordKind.Window {
                    continue
                }
                let device = bound_device(&bound, process.name, record.name)
                add_device_row(&var rows, &board, device, first)
            }
        }
        p = p + 1
    }
    var s = 0
    while s < image.setup.len() {
        let entry = image.setup.get(s)!
        add_device_row(&var rows, &board, entry.register.device, first)
        s = s + 1
    }
    var q = 0
    while q < image.pools.len() {
        let pool = image.pools.get(q)!
        try! rows.push(PlanRow(what: "the pool {pool.name}", kind: RegionKind.Pool, base: 0,
                               len: pool.len, pool: pool.name, heap: "", ram: pool.ram))
        q = q + 1
    }
    let heap_first = first + rows.len()
    var h = 0
    while h < bound.heaps.len() {
        let b = bound.heaps.get(h)!
        try! rows.push(PlanRow(what: "the heap {b.heap.name} of {b.process}", kind: RegionKind.Pool,
                               base: 0, len: b.heap.len, pool: "",
                               heap: "{b.process}.{b.heap.name}", ram: b.range))
        h = h + 1
    }

    // A connection per serve record, in image order and declaration order.
    var connections = Vector<String>()
    p = 0
    while p < count {
        let process = image.processes.get(p)!
        borrow let d = decls[p] {
            var r = 0
            while r < d.records.len() {
                let record = d.records.get(r)!
                if record.kind == RecordKind.Serve {
                    try! connections.push("{process.name}.{record.name}")
                }
                r = r + 1
            }
        }
        p = p + 1
    }

    // The console's connection and the process serving it, which `bind`
    // holds to be a serve of this image.
    var console: Int? = None
    var console_server = ""
    if let target = image.console {
        console = index_of(&connections, target)
        console_server = target.substring(0, target.index_of(46)!)
    }

    var maps = Vector<UInt32>()
    p = 0
    while p < count {
        borrow let d = decls[p] {
            try! maps.push(bands_word(&d))
        }
        p = p + 1
    }
    try check_bands(&image, &decls, &maps, console_server, file)

    var children = Vector<PlanChild>()
    var lines = Vector<String>()
    var line_holders = Vector<String>()
    p = 0
    while p < count {
        let process = image.processes.get(p)!
        borrow let d = decls[p] {
            var records = Vector<PlanRecord>()
            var start = 0
            var r = 0
            while r < d.records.len() {
                let record = d.records.get(r)!
                r = r + 1
                var made = PlanRecord(tag: record.tag, source: Source.System, from: 0, offset: 0,
                                      len: 0, keep: d.keep_word(&record))
                match record.kind {
                    case System -> { start = record.tag },
                    case Window -> {
                        let w = bound_window(&bound, process.name, record.name)!
                        let device = board.device(w.device)!
                        made.from = (row_tag(&rows, first, w.device, "")!) as UInt64
                        if w.part {
                            made.source = Source.Carve
                            made.offset = w.base - device.base
                            made.len = w.len
                        } else {
                            made.source = Source.Row
                        }
                    },
                    case Line -> {
                        let name = bound_device(&bound, process.name, record.name)
                        let device = board.device(name)!
                        guard let line = device.line else {
                            return refused(file, process.at, "the line `{record.name}` of the process {process.name} is bound to {name}, which has no interrupt line")
                        }
                        let key = "{line}"
                        var k = 0
                        while k < lines.len() {
                            if (lines.get(k) ?? "").equals(key) {
                                return refused(file, process.at, "the processes {line_holders.get(k) ?? ""} and {process.name} both need the line {line} of {name}: the kernel binds a line once, to one holder")
                            }
                            k = k + 1
                        }
                        try! lines.push(key)
                        try! line_holders.push(process.name)
                        made.source = Source.Line
                        made.from = line as UInt64
                    },
                    case Serve -> {
                        made.source = Source.Outlet
                        made.from = (index_of(&connections, "{process.name}.{record.name}")!) as UInt64
                    },
                    case Client -> {
                        let target = image.entry(&image.clients, process.name, record.name)!
                        made.source = Source.Inlet
                        made.from = (index_of(&connections, target.value)!) as UInt64
                    },
                    case Memory -> {
                        let pool = image.entry(&image.pool_bindings, process.name, record.name)!
                        made.source = Source.Row
                        made.from = (row_tag(&rows, first, "", pool.value)!) as UInt64
                    }
                }
                try! records.push(made)
            }
            var floor = d.handle_floor()
            if let index = console {
                if not process.name.equals(console_server) {
                    try check_console_inlet(&d, process.name, file, process.at)
                    try! records.push(PlanRecord(tag: CONSOLE_TAG as Int, source: Source.Inlet,
                                                 from: index as UInt64, offset: 0, len: 0,
                                                 keep: console_keep(&d)))
                    floor = floor + 1
                }
            }
            var k = 0
            while k < bound.heaps.len() {
                let b = bound.heaps.get(k)!
                if b.process.equals(process.name) {
                    try! records.push(PlanRecord(tag: (HEAP_TAG as Int) + b.heap.slot,
                                                 source: Source.Heap,
                                                 from: (heap_first + k) as UInt64, offset: 0,
                                                 len: 0, keep: KEEP_ALL))
                }
                k = k + 1
            }
            let quota = try quota_rows(&image, &d, process.name, process.at)
            try! children.push(PlanChild(name: process.name, image: p, destination: count + p,
                                         quota: move quota, ceilings: ceiling_rows(&d),
                                         bands: bands_word(&d),
                                         records: move records,
                                         rights: d.system_rights_or(&image.system_rights),
                                         start: start,
                                         shutdown: process.on_exit.equals("shutdown"),
                                         floor: floor, windows: d.window_count(),
                                         heaps: d.heaps.len()))
        }
        p = p + 1
    }
    last_takers(&var children)

    var setup = Vector<PlanSetup>()
    let window = if grain > REGISTER_BYTES { grain } else { REGISTER_BYTES }
    s = 0
    while s < image.setup.len() {
        let entry = image.setup.get(s)!
        s = s + 1
        let device = board.device(entry.register.device)!
        let at = entry.register.base - device.base
        let offset = at / window * window
        try! setup.push(PlanSetup(register: entry.reference, row: row_tag(&rows, first, device.name, "")!,
                                  offset: offset, len: window, at: at - offset, op: entry.op,
                                  value: entry.value))
    }
    return ImagePlan(children: move children, setup: move setup,
                     connections: connections.len(), rows: move rows, windows: None)
}

/// The packed band map `d`'s mode gives.
func bands_word(d: &Declaration) -> UInt32 {
    if d.full_bands {
        return FULL_BANDS
    }
    SIMPLE_BANDS
}

/// `Normal`'s level in the band map `map`.
func normal_level(map: UInt32) -> Int {
    ((map >> 8) & 0xF) as Int
}

/// The process of `image` named `name`'s index, or -1.
func process_index(image: &ImageFile, name: String) -> Int {
    var s = 0
    while s < image.processes.len() {
        if (image.processes.get(s)!).name.equals(name) {
            return s
        }
        s = s + 1
    }
    -1
}

/// Refuses a client whose `Normal` level is above its server's, the
/// convention that stands in for a server inheriting its client's level across
/// a pipe. `maps` is each process's band map, in image order; a client is a
/// declared `client` record and, in an image that names a console, every
/// process but the one serving it (`console_server`, "" when there is none).
/// The two stock maps put `Normal` at 2, so no declaration's mode can fail it;
/// it guards a map the plan carries from elsewhere.
public func check_bands(image: &ImageFile, decls: &Vector<Declaration>, maps: &Vector<UInt32>,
                        console_server: String, file: String) -> Result<Void, BuildError> {
    var p = 0
    while p < image.processes.len() {
        let process = image.processes.get(p)!
        let mine = normal_level(maps.get(p)!)
        borrow let d = decls[p] {
            var r = 0
            while r < d.records.len() {
                let record = d.records.get(r)!
                r = r + 1
                if record.kind != RecordKind.Client {
                    continue
                }
                let target = image.entry(&image.clients, process.name, record.name)!
                let server = target.value.substring(0, target.value.index_of(46)!)
                let theirs = normal_level(maps.get(process_index(&image, server))!)
                if mine > theirs {
                    return refused(file, process.at, "the process {process.name}'s `Normal` band is at level {mine}, above level {theirs}, its server {server}'s, which it is a client of through {target.value}: a client's `Normal` level may not be above its server's")
                }
            }
        }
        if not console_server.is_empty() && not process.name.equals(console_server) {
            let theirs = normal_level(maps.get(process_index(&image, console_server))!)
            if mine > theirs {
                return refused(file, process.at, "the process {process.name}'s `Normal` band is at level {mine}, above level {theirs}, the console server {console_server}'s, whose connection it is given an inlet of: a client's `Normal` level may not be above its server's")
            }
        }
        p = p + 1
    }
    return
}

/// The ceilings root narrows a child to for `d`: each kind's word, in the
/// table's order, when `d` has `[ceilings]`.
func ceiling_rows(d: &Declaration) -> Vector<PlanCeiling> {
    var out = Vector<PlanCeiling>()
    if not d.has_ceilings {
        return move out
    }
    var i = 0
    while i < CEILING_KINDS {
        let info = ceiling_kind_at(i)
        try! out.push(PlanCeiling(kind: info.case_name, rights: d.ceiling_word(info.key)))
        i = i + 1
    }
    move out
}

/// The keep word of the console's inlet in `d`'s process: its `pipe-inlet`
/// ceiling when it has one, as any inlet record without `rights` has, and
/// every right the inlet holds otherwise.
func console_keep(d: &Declaration) -> UInt32 {
    if d.has_ceilings {
        return d.ceiling_word("pipe-inlet")
    }
    KEEP_ALL
}

/// Refuses a process whose `pipe-inlet` ceiling withholds `post` in an image
/// that gives it the console's inlet: its runtime posts every line it prints
/// through it.
func check_console_inlet(d: &Declaration, process: String, file: String,
                         at: TomlPosition) -> Result<Void, BuildError> {
    if not d.has_ceilings {
        return
    }
    let info = ceiling_kind("pipe-inlet")!
    if (d.ceiling_word("pipe-inlet") & (right_word(&info, "post") ?? 0)) == 0 {
        return refused(file, at, "the process {process}'s `pipe-inlet` ceiling in [ceilings] lacks `post`: the runtime posts every line the process prints through the console's inlet, and this image gives it one")
    }
    return
}

/// The device bound to the need `need` of `process`.
func bound_device(bound: &Bindings, process: String, need: String) -> String {
    (bound_window(&bound, process, need)!).device
}

/// The window bound to the need `need` of `process`.
func bound_window(bound: &Bindings, process: String, need: String) -> Window? {
    var i = 0
    while i < bound.windows.len() {
        let b = bound.windows.get(i)!
        if b.process.equals(process) && b.need.equals(need) {
            return b.window
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    None
}

/// A row for `device`, unless it has one.
func add_device_row(rows: &var Vector<PlanRow>, board: &Board, device: String, first: Int) {
    if row_tag(&rows, first, device, "") != None {
        return
    }
    let d = board.device(device)!
    try! rows.push(PlanRow(what: device, kind: RegionKind.Device, base: d.base, len: d.len,
                           pool: "", heap: "", ram: ""))
}

/// The index of `name` in `names`.
func index_of(names: &Vector<String>, name: String) -> Int? {
    var i = 0
    while i < names.len() {
        if (names.get(i) ?? "").equals(name) {
            return i
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    None
}

/// Each whole window given as its row's sibling, but the last record that
/// takes its row when nothing after it carves or takes that row: that one is
/// the row.
func last_takers(children: &var Vector<PlanChild>) {
    var c = 0
    while c < children.len() {
        var r = 0
        var count = 0
        borrow let child = children[c] {
            count = child.records.len()
        }
        while r < count {
            var record = PlanRecord(tag: 0, source: Source.System, from: 0, offset: 0, len: 0,
                                    keep: KEEP_ALL)
            borrow let child = children[c] {
                record = child.records.get(r)!
            }
            if record.source == Source.Row && later_use(&children, c, r, record.from) {
                borrow var child = children[c] {
                    child.records[r] = PlanRecord(tag: record.tag, source: Source.Sibling,
                                                  from: record.from, offset: 0, len: 0,
                                                  keep: record.keep)
                }
            }
            r = r + 1
        }
        c = c + 1
    }
}

/// Whether a record after child `c`'s record `r` takes the row `row`.
func later_use(children: &Vector<PlanChild>, c: Int, r: Int, row: UInt64) -> Bool {
    var i = c
    while i < children.len() {
        borrow let child = children[i] {
            var j = if i == c { r + 1 } else { 0 }
            while j < child.records.len() {
                let other = child.records.get(j)!
                let takes = other.source == Source.Row || other.source == Source.Sibling ||
                            other.source == Source.Carve
                if takes && other.from == row {
                    return true
                }
                j = j + 1
            }
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    false
}

/// A process's quota rows, in kind order: its declaration's, each replaced by
/// the image's, which may not lower one.
func quota_rows(image: &ImageFile, d: &Declaration, process: String,
                at: TomlPosition) -> Result<Vector<PlanQuota>, BuildError> {
    var limits = Vector<Int>()
    var k = 0
    while k < QUOTA_KINDS {
        try! limits.push(-1)
        k = k + 1
    }
    var declared = Vector<Bool>()
    k = 0
    while k < QUOTA_KINDS {
        try! declared.push(false)
        k = k + 1
    }
    var i = 0
    while i < d.quota.len() {
        let row = d.quota.get(i)!
        limits[quota_of(row.name)] = row.value
        declared[quota_of(row.name)] = true
        i = i + 1
    }
    i = 0
    while i < image.quotas.len() {
        let given = image.quotas.get(i)!
        i = i + 1
        if not given.process.equals(process) {
            continue
        }
        let kind = quota_of(given.key)
        let value = given.value.to_int() ?? 0
        if kind == QUOTA_THREAD && value == 0 {
            return refused(image.file, given.at, "the image gives the process {process} `threads` = 0: a process's first thread is charged to its row, and with none it cannot start")
        }
        let stated = limits.get(kind) ?? -1
        if value < stated {
            return refused(image.file, given.at, "the image gives the process {process} `{given.key}` = {value}, below the {stated} its declaration ({d.file}) needs")
        }
        limits[kind] = value
    }
    var out = Vector<PlanQuota>()
    k = 0
    while k < QUOTA_KINDS {
        let limit = limits.get(k) ?? -1
        if limit >= 0 {
            try! out.push(PlanQuota(kind: k, limit: limit, declared: declared.get(k) ?? false))
        }
        k = k + 1
    }
    move out
}

/// Holds `plan` to the kernel `facts` describes, for an image named by `what`
/// whose children start with the quota rows `defaults` (by `QuotaKind`
/// value) and whose slabs hold `slabs`: each quota row against its bound,
/// and a row the image alone gives against the row it would lower; each
/// child's `Handle` row against what it holds when it starts and once its
/// heaps have grown, its `Mapping` row against its windows and heaps and its
/// `Memory` row against its heaps; root at every step of the plan, its
/// handle table against the longest one and the objects it has made of each
/// kind `slabs` counts. Answers what the plan asks of the handle tables, boot
/// sets and slabs (`PlanNeeds`).
public func check_plan(plan: &ImagePlan, facts: &KernelFacts, defaults: &Vector<Int>,
                       slabs: &PlanSlabs, what: String) -> Result<PlanNeeds, BuildError> {
    var needs = PlanNeeds.none()
    needs.stock = true
    var k = 0
    while k < SLAB_KINDS {
        try! needs.summed.push(0)
        k = k + 1
    }
    var c = 0
    while c < plan.children.len() {
        borrow let child = plan.children[c] {
            let row = try check_child(&child, &facts, &defaults, what)
            add_rows(&var needs, &child)
            try! needs.names.push(child.name)
            try! needs.rows.push(row)
            try! needs.records.push(child.records.len())
        }
        c = c + 1
    }
    let longest = facts.handles + facts.table_blocks * facts.handle_block
    let peak = try root_steps(&plan, longest, &slabs, what)
    needs.held = peak.held
    needs.step = peak.step
    return move needs
}

/// Adds what `child`'s rows ask of each slab to `needs.summed`: each quota row
/// that draws on a slab, a Thread row of its own or one for its main thread,
/// and at least its heaps' Memory objects, which its `Memory` row covers.
func add_rows(needs: &var PlanNeeds, child: &PlanChild) {
    var threads = 1
    var memories = child.heaps
    var q = 0
    while q < child.quota.len() {
        let row = child.quota.get(q)!
        q = q + 1
        let slab = quota_slab(row.kind)
        if slab < 0 {
            continue
        }
        if slab == THREADS {
            threads = row.limit
        } else if slab == MEMORIES {
            if row.limit > memories {
                memories = row.limit
            }
        } else {
            needs.summed[slab] = (needs.summed.get(slab) ?? 0) + row.limit
        }
    }
    needs.summed[THREADS] = (needs.summed.get(THREADS) ?? 0) + threads
    needs.summed[MEMORIES] = (needs.summed.get(MEMORIES) ?? 0) + memories
}

/// `check_plan` for one child; answers its `Handle` row.
func check_child(child: &PlanChild, facts: &KernelFacts, defaults: &Vector<Int>,
                 what: String) -> Result<Int, BuildError> {
    let mapping_bound = facts.budget - facts.image_rows
    var handles = defaults.get(QUOTA_HANDLE) ?? 0
    var mappings = defaults.get(QUOTA_MAPPING) ?? 0
    var memories = defaults.get(QUOTA_MEMORY) ?? 0
    var q = 0
    while q < child.quota.len() {
        let row = child.quota.get(q)!
        q = q + 1
        let key = quota_key(row.kind)
        if row.limit >= QUOTA_UNLIMITED {
            return BuildError(message: "{what}: the process {child.name}'s `{key}` row is {row.limit}, which the ledger's row cannot hold below its unlimited mark ({QUOTA_UNLIMITED})")
        }
        let boots = defaults.get(row.kind) ?? 0
        if not row.declared && row.limit < boots {
            return BuildError(message: "{what}: the image gives the process {child.name} `{key}` = {row.limit}, below the {boots} the image's children start with: an image raises a row and never lowers one")
        }
        if row.kind == QUOTA_HANDLE {
            let longest = facts.handles + facts.table_blocks * facts.handle_block
            if row.limit > longest {
                return BuildError(message: "{what}: the process {child.name}'s `handles` row is {row.limit}, past the longest handle table ({longest})")
            }
            handles = row.limit
        }
        if row.kind == QUOTA_MAPPING && row.limit > mapping_bound {
            return BuildError(message: "{what}: the process {child.name}'s `mappings` row is {row.limit}, past the {mapping_bound} grant rows an image leaves of this board's {facts.budget}")
        }
        if row.kind == QUOTA_MAPPING {
            mappings = row.limit
        }
        if row.kind == QUOTA_MEMORY {
            memories = row.limit
        }
    }
    if mappings < child.windows + child.heaps {
        return BuildError(message: "{what}: the process {child.name}'s `Mapping` row is {mappings}, short of the {child.windows + child.heaps} rows it maps, one for each window ({child.windows}) and each heap ({child.heaps})")
    }
    if memories < child.heaps {
        return BuildError(message: "{what}: the process {child.name}'s `Memory` row is {memories}, short of the {child.heaps} its heaps hold, one each")
    }
    if handles < child.floor && child.heaps > 0 {
        return BuildError(message: "{what}: the process {child.name}'s `Handle` row is {handles}, short of the {child.floor} handles it holds once its {child.heaps} heaps have grown")
    }
    if handles < child.floor {
        if has_console(&child) {
            return BuildError(message: "{what}: the process {child.name}'s `Handle` row is {handles}, short of the {child.floor} handles it holds when it starts, the console's inlet under CONSOLE_TAG among them")
        }
        return BuildError(message: "{what}: the process {child.name}'s `Handle` row is {handles}, short of the {child.floor} handles it holds when it starts")
    }
    return handles
}

/// Whether `child` is given the console's inlet.
func has_console(child: &PlanChild) -> Bool {
    var r = 0
    while r < child.records.len() {
        let record = child.records.get(r)!
        if record.tag == CONSOLE_TAG as Int && record.source == Source.Inlet {
            return true
        }
        r = r + 1
    }
    false
}

/// Refuses a step of `plan` at which root would hold more than `table` handles,
/// the longest handle table, and answers the most it holds at any step and the
/// first step it holds that at. Root takes handles as `root/` does: its boot
/// handles and one per row, the Process handle and the main thread's own Thread
/// handle its start-up derives, each child created and its two rows released,
/// each setup write's carve and mapping, each record made and given, and its
/// Waiter, made before it releases what is left of the rows and connections.
/// Refuses one at which the objects of a kind would number more than `slabs`
/// holds: Process objects, root's and one for each child created; IoMemory
/// objects, one per device row, made at boot, one for each setup write's carve
/// while it is written, and one for each carve given; a Pipe for each
/// connection made; and an Interrupt for each line bound.
func root_steps(plan: &ImagePlan, table: Int, slabs: &PlanSlabs,
                what: String) -> Result<Peak, BuildError> {
    let count = plan.children.len()
    var devices = 0
    var d = 0
    while d < plan.rows.len() {
        if (plan.rows.get(d)!).kind == RegionKind.Device {
            devices = devices + 1
        }
        d = d + 1
    }
    var steps = Steps(held: ROOT_BOOT_HANDLES + 2 * count + plan.rows.len() +
                            ROOT_START_HANDLES,
                      made: Vector<Bool>(), iomemories: devices, pipes: 0, interrupts: 0,
                      slabs: slabs, peak: 0, step: "")
    try steps.within(0, table, what, "derive")
    var c = 0
    while c < count {
        borrow let child = plan.children[c] {
            let step = "create {child.name}"
            try steps.within(1, table, what, step)
            try objects_within(c + 2, slabs.processes, "Process", what, step)
        }
        steps.held = steps.held - 1
        c = c + 1
    }
    var s = 0
    while s < plan.setup.len() {
        let step = "setup {(plan.setup.get(s)!).register}"
        try steps.within(2, table, what, step)
        try objects_within(steps.iomemories + 1, slabs.iomemories, "IoMemory", what,
                           step)
        s = s + 1
    }
    var k = 0
    while k < plan.connections {
        try! steps.made.push(false)
        k = k + 1
    }
    c = 0
    while c < count {
        borrow let child = plan.children[c] {
            var r = 0
            while r < child.records.len() {
                let record = child.records.get(r)!
                r = r + 1
                try give_step(&var steps, &record, table, what,
                              "give {child.name} record {record.tag}")
            }
        }
        c = c + 1
    }
    try steps.within(1, table, what, "supervise")
    return Peak(held: steps.peak, step: steps.step)
}

/// The most handles root holds at any step, and the first step it holds that
/// many at.
struct Peak {
    held: Int
    step: String
}

/// What root holds as `root_steps` walks the plan, which connections it has
/// made, and how many IoMemory, Pipe and Interrupt objects there are of the
/// image's `slabs`.
struct Steps {
    held: Int
    made: Vector<Bool>
    iomemories: Int
    pipes: Int
    interrupts: Int
    slabs: PlanSlabs
    /// The most root has held at a step so far, and the first step that held
    /// it.
    peak: Int
    step: String
}

@synthesize
extension Steps: ExplicitCopy {}

/// One record made and given, at `step`.
func give_step(steps: &var Steps, record: &PlanRecord, table: Int, what: String,
               step: String) -> Result<Void, BuildError> {
    match record.source {
        case Row -> { steps.held = steps.held - 1 },
        case Heap -> { steps.held = steps.held - 1 },
        case Outlet -> {
            try connect(&var steps, record.from as Int, table, what, step)
            steps.held = steps.held - 1
        },
        case Inlet -> {
            try connect(&var steps, record.from as Int, table, what, step)
            try steps.within(1, table, what, step)
        },
        case Carve -> {
            steps.iomemories = steps.iomemories + 1
            try objects_within(steps.iomemories, steps.slabs.iomemories, "IoMemory", what,
                               step)
        },
        case Line -> {
            steps.interrupts = steps.interrupts + 1
            try objects_within(steps.interrupts, steps.slabs.interrupts, "Interrupt", what,
                               step)
        },
        // A System sibling, a row's sibling, a carve's handle or a line's is
        // made and given at once, and never takes root's table past a step
        // before it: root held at least one more at its first create, and
        // since the last connection it made it has held no more than it held
        // then.
        case _ -> {}
    }
    return
}

/// Connection `index` made, if it is not yet.
func connect(steps: &var Steps, index: Int, table: Int, what: String,
             step: String) -> Result<Void, BuildError> {
    if steps.made.get(index) ?? true {
        return
    }
    steps.made[index] = true
    steps.held = steps.held + 2
    try steps.within(0, table, what, step)
    steps.pipes = steps.pipes + 1
    objects_within(steps.pipes, steps.slabs.pipes, "Pipe", what, step)
}

/// Refuses `objects` objects of `kind` past the slab's `slab` at `step`.
func objects_within(objects: Int, slab: Int, kind: String, what: String,
                    step: String) -> Result<Void, BuildError> {
    if objects > slab {
        return BuildError(message: "{what}: the stock root would make the {kind} objects {objects} at `{step}`, past the image's {slab}")
    }
    return
}

extension Steps {
    /// Notes root holding `extra` handles more than it does now at `step`,
    /// and refuses them past `table`, the longest handle table.
    func within(&var self, extra: Int, table: Int, what: String,
                step: String) -> Result<Void, BuildError> {
        let held = self.held + extra
        if held > table {
            return BuildError(message: "{what}: the stock root would hold {held} handles at `{step}`, past the longest handle table ({table})")
        }
        if held > self.peak {
            self.peak = held
            self.step = step
        }
        return
    }
}

extension ImagePlan {
    /// Reads a test image's plan, `fields`.
    public static func read(fields: &var Fields) -> Result<ImagePlan, BuildError> {
        var children = Vector<PlanChild>()
        var given = try fields.objects_or_empty("children", "a plan's child")
        var c = 0
        while c < given.len() {
            borrow var f = given[c] {
                try! children.push(try read_child(&var f))
            }
            c = c + 1
        }
        var setup = Vector<PlanSetup>()
        var writes = try fields.objects_or_empty("setup", "a plan's setup write")
        var s = 0
        while s < writes.len() {
            borrow var f = writes[s] {
                let word = try f.text("op")
                let op = if word.equals("set") { SetupOp.Set } else if word.equals("clear") {
                    SetupOp.Clear
                } else if word.equals("write") { SetupOp.Write } else {
                    return BuildError(message: "a plan's setup write has the op `{word}`, not one of `set`, `clear`, `write`")
                }
                try! setup.push(PlanSetup(register: try f.text("register"), row: try f.integer("row"),
                                          offset: try f.word("offset"), len: try f.word("len"),
                                          at: try f.word("at"), op: op, value: try f.word("value")))
                try f.finish()
            }
            s = s + 1
        }
        var connections = 0
        if fields.has("connections") {
            connections = try fields.integer("connections")
        }
        var windows: Int? = None
        if fields.has("windows") {
            windows = try fields.integer("windows")
        }
        try fields.finish()
        return ImagePlan(children: move children, setup: move setup, connections: connections,
                         rows: Vector<PlanRow>(), windows: windows)
    }
}

/// One child of a test image's plan.
func read_child(f: &var Fields) -> Result<PlanChild, BuildError> {
    let name = try f.text("name")
    var quota = Vector<PlanQuota>()
    if var q = try f.object("quota", "a plan child's `quota`") {
        let keys = quota_keys()
        var k = 0
        while k < keys.len() {
            let key = keys.get(k) ?? ""
            if q.has(key) {
                try! quota.push(PlanQuota(kind: quota_of(key), limit: try q.integer(key),
                                         declared: true))
            }
            k = k + 1
        }
        try q.finish()
    }
    var ceilings = Vector<PlanCeiling>()
    if var c = try f.object("ceilings", "a plan child's `ceilings`") {
        var k = 0
        while k < CEILING_KINDS {
            let info = ceiling_kind_at(k)
            if c.has(info.key) {
                try! ceilings.push(PlanCeiling(kind: info.case_name,
                                               rights: (try c.word(info.key)) as UInt32))
            }
            k = k + 1
        }
        try c.finish()
    }
    var bands: UInt64 = SIMPLE_BANDS as UInt64
    if f.has("bands") {
        bands = try f.word("bands")
    }
    var records = Vector<PlanRecord>()
    var given = try f.objects_or_empty("records", "a plan child's record")
    var r = 0
    while r < given.len() {
        borrow var g = given[r] {
            let word = try g.text("source")
            guard let source = source_named(word) else {
                return BuildError(message: "a plan's record has the source `{word}`, not one of `system`, `row`, `sibling`, `carve`, `line`, `outlet`, `inlet`, `heap`")
            }
            var from: UInt64 = 0
            var offset: UInt64 = 0
            var len: UInt64 = 0
            var keep: UInt64 = KEEP_ALL as UInt64
            if g.has("from") { from = try g.word("from") }
            if g.has("offset") { offset = try g.word("offset") }
            if g.has("len") { len = try g.word("len") }
            if g.has("keep") { keep = try g.word("keep") }
            try! records.push(PlanRecord(tag: try g.integer("tag"), source: source, from: from,
                                         offset: offset, len: len, keep: keep as UInt32))
            try g.finish()
        }
        r = r + 1
    }
    var shutdown = false
    if f.has("shutdown") {
        shutdown = try f.boolean("shutdown")
    }
    let child = PlanChild(name: name, image: try f.integer("image"),
                          destination: try f.integer("destination"), quota: move quota,
                          ceilings: move ceilings, bands: bands as UInt32,
                          records: move records, rights: child_rights(),
                          start: try f.integer("start"),
                          shutdown: shutdown, floor: 0, windows: 0, heaps: 0)
    try f.finish()
    return move child
}

/// `text` as a Saw string literal.
func literal(text: String) -> String {
    let quoted = text.replace("\\", "\\\\").replace("\"", "\\\"")
    let escaped = quoted.replace("\{", "\\\{").replace("\}", "\\\}")
    let quote = "\""
    "{quote}{escaped}{quote}"
}

/// The count of windows root is given for `plan`: the one a test plan
/// states, or `window_rows`.
public func root_windows(plan: &ImagePlan) -> Int {
    plan.windows ?? window_rows(&plan)
}

/// How many device rows root holds as windows, at most: each row a sibling
/// or carve record or a setup write names, which root takes as a window the
/// first time it is named.
public func window_rows(plan: &ImagePlan) -> Int {
    var rows = Vector<UInt64>()
    var s = 0
    while s < plan.setup.len() {
        note_row(&var rows, (plan.setup.get(s)!).row as UInt64)
        s = s + 1
    }
    var c = 0
    while c < plan.children.len() {
        borrow let child = plan.children[c] {
            var r = 0
            while r < child.records.len() {
                let record = child.records.get(r)!
                if record.source == Source.Sibling || record.source == Source.Carve {
                    note_row(&var rows, record.from)
                }
                r = r + 1
            }
        }
        c = c + 1
    }
    rows.len()
}

/// `row` added to `rows` unless it is there.
func note_row(rows: &var Vector<UInt64>, row: UInt64) {
    var k = 0
    while k < rows.len() {
        if (rows.get(k) ?? 0) == row {
            return
        }
        k = k + 1
    }
    try! rows.push(row)
}

/// The bytes the heap's block for a vector of `count` elements of `words`
/// words each takes, on a word of `word` bytes (`rt/common/src/heap.saw`): the
/// request and a one-word header, rounded up to two words and four at least.
/// An empty vector allocates nothing.
public func heap_block(count: Int, words: Int, word: Int) -> Int {
    if count <= 0 {
        return 0
    }
    let grain = 2 * word
    let need = (count * words * word + word + grain - 1) / grain * grain
    if need < 4 * word {
        return 4 * word
    }
    need
}

/// The blocks root's heap serves for `plan` on a word of `word` bytes: the
/// plan's vectors (`plan_module`) and root's bookkeeping (`root/`).
public func root_blocks(plan: &ImagePlan, word: Int) -> Int {
    var bytes = heap_block(plan.children.len(), CHILD_WORDS, word) +
                heap_block(plan.setup.len(), SETUP_WORDS, word)
    var c = 0
    while c < plan.children.len() {
        borrow let child = plan.children[c] {
            bytes = bytes + heap_block(child.quota.len(), QUOTA_WORDS, word) +
                    heap_block(child.ceilings.len(), CEILING_WORDS, word) +
                    heap_block(child.records.len(), RECORD_WORDS, word) +
                    heap_block(child.rights.len(), RIGHT_WORDS, word)
        }
        c = c + 1
    }
    let windows = root_windows(&plan)
    bytes + heap_block(plan.children.len(), PROCESS_WORDS, word) +
        heap_block(plan.connections, ENDS_WORDS, word) +
        heap_block(windows, ROW_TAG_WORDS, word) +
        heap_block(windows, ROW_WINDOW_WORDS, word)
}

/// The bytes ahead of a heap's first block in a region of `size` bytes whose
/// start is aligned to two words (`rt/common/src/heap.saw`): the control
/// block, sized for a block as large as the region, and the first block's
/// header, rounded up to two words.
public func heap_front(size: Int, word: Int) -> Int {
    let classes = heap_classes(size as UInt64, word)
    let grain = 2 * word
    let words = HEAP_CONTROL_FIXED + classes * HEAP_CLASS_WORDS
    (words * word + word + grain - 1) / grain * grain
}

/// The arena the stock root is linked with for `plan` on a word of `word`
/// bytes: its heap's front, the blocks it serves and `ROOT_ARENA_MARGIN`,
/// rounded up to `ARENA_ALIGN` and no less than `ROOT_ARENA_FLOOR`.
public func root_arena(plan: &ImagePlan, word: Int) -> UInt64 {
    let blocks = root_blocks(&plan, word)
    var size = ROOT_ARENA_FLOOR
    var need = arena_need(size, blocks, word)
    // The front grows with the region, so a larger size is measured again.
    while need > size {
        size = need
        need = arena_need(size, blocks, word)
    }
    size as UInt64
}

/// What a region of `size` bytes must be to serve `blocks` bytes of blocks
/// and keep `ROOT_ARENA_MARGIN`, rounded up to `ARENA_ALIGN`.
func arena_need(size: Int, blocks: Int, word: Int) -> Int {
    let total = heap_front(size, word) + blocks + ROOT_ARENA_MARGIN
    (total + ARENA_ALIGN - 1) / ARENA_ALIGN * ARENA_ALIGN
}

/// The module `imageplan` for `plan`, as the lines of its `lib.saw`; `name`
/// names the image. Each vector is made at its length, so none grows.
public func plan_module(plan: &ImagePlan, name: String) -> Vector<String> {
    var out = Vector<String>()
    try! out.push("//! Generated by sosimage: the stock root's plan for the image {name}.")
    try! out.push("")
    try! out.push("import bootplan.\{Plan, Child, Record, Source, Setup, SetupOp, Quota, QuotaName, RightName,
                 Ceiling, CeilingKind\}")
    try! out.push("")
    try! out.push("public func plan() -> Plan \{")
    try! out.push("    var children = try! Vector<Child>(capacity: {plan.children.len()})")
    var c = 0
    while c < plan.children.len() {
        try! out.push("    try! children.push(child_{c}())")
        c = c + 1
    }
    try! out.push("    var setup = try! Vector<Setup>(capacity: {plan.setup.len()})")
    var s = 0
    while s < plan.setup.len() {
        let w = plan.setup.get(s)!
        let op = match w.op { case Set -> "Set", case Clear -> "Clear", case Write -> "Write" }
        try! out.push("    try! setup.push(Setup(register: {literal(w.register)}, row: {w.row}, offset: {hex(w.offset)}, len: {hex(w.len)}, at: {hex(w.at)}, op: SetupOp.{op}, value: {hex(w.value)}))")
        s = s + 1
    }
    try! out.push("    Plan(children: move children, setup: move setup, connections: {plan.connections},")
    try! out.push("         windows: {root_windows(&plan)})")
    try! out.push("\}")
    c = 0
    while c < plan.children.len() {
        borrow let child = plan.children[c] {
            try! out.append(&child_function(&child, c))
        }
        c = c + 1
    }
    move out
}

/// The function `plan_module` writes for child `index`.
func child_function(child: &PlanChild, index: Int) -> Vector<String> {
    var out = Vector<String>()
    try! out.push("")
    try! out.push("func child_{index}() -> Child \{")
    try! out.push("    var quota = try! Vector<Quota>(capacity: {child.quota.len()})")
    var q = 0
    while q < child.quota.len() {
        let row = child.quota.get(q)!
        try! out.push("    try! quota.push(Quota(kind: QuotaName.{quota_name(row.kind)}, limit: {row.limit}))")
        q = q + 1
    }
    try! out.push("    var ceilings = try! Vector<Ceiling>(capacity: {child.ceilings.len()})")
    var c = 0
    while c < child.ceilings.len() {
        let ceiling = child.ceilings.get(c)!
        try! out.push("    try! ceilings.push(Ceiling(kind: CeilingKind.{ceiling.kind}, rights: {hex(ceiling.rights as UInt64)}))")
        c = c + 1
    }
    try! out.push("    var records = try! Vector<Record>(capacity: {child.records.len()})")
    var r = 0
    while r < child.records.len() {
        let record = child.records.get(r)!
        try! out.push("    try! records.push(Record(tag: {record.tag}, source: Source.{source_word(record.source)}, from: {hex(record.from)}, offset: {hex(record.offset)}, len: {hex(record.len)}, keep: {hex(record.keep as UInt64)}))")
        r = r + 1
    }
    try! out.push("    var rights = try! Vector<RightName>(capacity: {child.rights.len()})")
    var k = 0
    while k < child.rights.len() {
        try! out.push("    try! rights.push(RightName.{right_word(child.rights.get(k) ?? "")})")
        k = k + 1
    }
    try! out.push("    Child(name: {literal(child.name)}, image: {child.image}, destination: {child.destination},")
    try! out.push("          quota: move quota, ceilings: move ceilings, bands: {hex(child.bands as UInt64)},")
    try! out.push("          records: move records,")
    try! out.push("          rights: move rights,")
    try! out.push("          start: {child.start}, shutdown: {child.shutdown})")
    try! out.push("\}")
    move out
}
